 "pg_test_fsync_raw": "5 seconds per test\nO_DIRECT supported on this platform for open_datasync and open_sync.\n\nCompare file sync methods using one 8kB write:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      4621.965 ops/sec     216 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          4529.994 ops/sec     221 usecs/op\n        fsync                              4831.054 ops/sec     207 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          4797.073 ops/sec     208 usecs/op\n\nCompare file sync methods using two 8kB writes:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      4920.004 ops/sec     203 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          5111.660 ops/sec     196 usecs/op\n        fsync                              5104.891 ops/sec     196 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          4782.887 ops/sec     209 usecs/op\n\nCompare open_sync with different write sizes:\n(This is designed to compare the cost of writing 16kB in different write\nopen_sync sizes.)\n         1 * 16kB open_sync write          4931.300 ops/sec     203 usecs/op\n         2 *  8kB open_sync writes         4549.093 ops/sec     220 usecs/op\n         4 *  4kB open_sync writes         2969.924 ops/sec     337 usecs/op\n         8 *  2kB open_sync writes          883.245 ops/sec    1132 usecs/op\n        16 *  1kB open_sync writes          295.443 ops/sec    3385 usecs/op\n\nTest if fsync on non-write file descriptor is honored:\n(If the times are similar, fsync() can sync data written on a different\ndescriptor.)\n        write, fsync, close                3479.371 ops/sec     287 usecs/op\n        write, close, fsync                3416.994 ops/sec     293 usecs/op\n\nNon-sync'ed 8kB writes:\n        write                           1896835.165 ops/sec       1 usecs/op\n",
